[l_english.STATE_LORE_533]
If anything proves love outlasts hate, it is surely the Apple-Pear Tree. This peculiar tree—one half of its branches bearing crisp red apples, the other laden with golden pears—stubbornly thrives. It stands silently beside the ruins of the old Pear family homestead, as if whispering a love story long lost to time.
Previously, the Pear family rarely spoke of the past, especially not of their rebellious daughter who married into the rival Apple clan. Later, the Pear family often spoke of that tree, as it was a story of freely pursued love, and of reconciliation and harmony triumphing over hatred. And then, they stopped speaking of it again, because concealing their connection to the Apple family became their only way to protect themselves, and both families.
Yet, in the quiet of night, the Pear ponies invariably find their gaze drawn to that unique tree. They don’t approach it; they simply watch from afar, feeling the faint glow it emits in the darkness. This luminescence isn’t magic, but pure, untainted affection, accompanied by the endless loneliness.

[l_simp_chinese.STATE_LORE_533]
如果说有什么能证明爱比恨更长久，那一定是梨苹果树。这棵奇特的树，一半枝丫结出鲜红的苹果，另一半则挂满金黄的梨子，却依然顽强地生长着。它静静地矗立在梨家族旧宅的废墟旁，仿佛在低声诉说着一个早已被时间尘封的爱情故事。
此前梨家族的成员们很少谈及过去，尤其是那个与宿敌苹果家族联姻的叛逆女儿。后来梨家族们常常谈起那棵树，那是一个关于自由追逐爱情、和解与和谐超越仇恨的故事。再后来他们又不再谈起那棵树了，因为隐瞒与苹果家族的关系使他们保护自己，也是保护两个家族的唯一方法。
然而，每当夜晚的月光洒下，梨家族的马群们总会不自觉地望向那棵独特的树。他们不会靠近，只是远远地，在黑暗中感受它散发出的微弱光芒。那光芒并非来自魔法，而是纯粹的、未被污染的爱意，以及随之而来的，那份无尽的孤独与失落。
